3. Remote Dashboard - local-network HTTP server for mobile/PC browser dashboards (finalized scope):
   V1 - Read-only JSON endpoints + built-in mobile dashboard HTML page served at /:
     GET /api/status, /api/score, /api/rate, /api/qsos?limit=N&offset=N,
         /api/rig, /api/mults, /api/propagation
     Single-file static HTML+JS dashboard auto-refreshing every 5s, token via
     ?token= query param for bookmarkable URL.
   V2 - Minimal rig-control writes - SHIPPED 0.7.25 (no QSO logging, no CW memory trigger):
     POST /api/rig/qsy { radio, freq_hz, mode }
     POST /api/rig/band { radio, band }
     POST /api/rig/run_mode { radio, mode: Run|S&P|Off }
   V3+ (explicitly deferred): POST /api/qso, POST /api/cw/memory - both race
     with keyboard focus, not worth the risk.
   Infrastructure:
     - Qt6::HttpServer module (add to CMakeLists + install-qt-action modules)
     - Dedicated QThread for the server so slow clients can't hiccup the UI
     - Auth: single token, Authorization: Bearer <t> or ?token= query param
     - Bind: LAN-only default, Preferences offers 127.0.0.1-only or specific iface
     - Preferences UI: enable toggle, port, bind mode, token + Copy-URL-for-Phone
       button, Rotate Token button
     - Discovery handled via QR code in Preferences (shipped 0.7.25 using
       nayuki's qrcodegen under third_party/). Operator scans with phone
       camera; no mDNS responder needed, no Bonjour-on-Windows burden.

4. Multi-Multi networked operation - peer-to-peer CLX coordination across multiple
   stations on the same LAN. Each station runs its own CLX; instances discover each
   other (mDNS, shared with item 3) and coordinate via UDP multicast for real-time
   push (QSOs, band state) and HTTP/RPC for request-response (serial number draws,
   full log sync on join).
   V1 scope (minimum viable M/M):
     - Peer discovery via mDNS (reuse item 3's infra): _contestlogx-mm._udp.local
     - QSO broadcast on log: every peer mirrors others' QSOs into a read-only
       "peer log" used for dupe check but NOT scored locally
     - Band-lock advisory: visual indicator showing which band each peer is on;
       warn (not block) on band collision. Blocking is a policy call.
     - Shared serial numbers: single-master election (lowest node ID / configurable
       override); peers request next serial via HTTP POST /api/mm/serial. Master
       death triggers re-election; in-flight draws reconcile on rejoin.
     - Station identity: op callsign + position name (e.g. "K1ABC/Run-1") baked
       into every peer message
     - Dupe check considers local + peer logs; scorer continues to score local only
   V2 scope:
     - Full log sync on join (station reconnects after disconnect; asks peers for
       QSOs since last-known timestamp)
     - Durable peer-log persistence so dupes survive restart
     - Real-time score aggregation (captain's dashboard showing per-station
       contribution and running total)
     - HMAC signing of multicast packets with shared network secret to block
       rogue CLX instances or neighbouring stations on the same subnet
   V3+:
     - Full band-lock enforcement (refuse to tune, not just warn)
     - Cross-station spot sharing from DX cluster
     - Encrypted peer channel for non-trusted networks
   Design anchors:
     - Message format: JSON over UDP multicast (group 239.x.x.x, port configurable);
       each packet has node_id, sequence, timestamp, payload
     - Same QThread that runs the HTTP server hosts the multicast listener/sender
     - Shares thread-safe QSO snapshot struct with items 3 (HTTP) and onlineScoreClient
     - Failure mode priority: never lose a local QSO; dropped peer messages are
       recovered via the sync-on-rejoin path
